{"model": "qwen3-coder-30b-a3b-bench", "created_at": "2026-09-11T19:19:52.536349073Z", "response": "1. First, calculate the cost of notebooks: 7 \u00d7 $4 = $28.\n   Then, calculate the cost of pens: 12 \u00d7 $1.50 = $18.\n   Total before discount: $28 + $18 = $46.\n   Discount: 10% of $46 = $4.60.\n   Final cost: $46 \u2212 $4.60 = $41.40.\n   ANSWER 1: 41.40\n\n2. In 4 years, Ben will be 30, so Ben is currently 26.\n   Let Cara\u2019s current age be C.\n   Six years ago, Cara was (C \u2212 6).\n   Ben is twice that age: 26 = 2(C \u2212 6).\n   Solving: 26 = 2C \u2212 12 \u2192 38 = 2C \u2192 C = 19.\n   Cara is 19 years old now.\n   ANSWER 2: 19\n\n3. Let's work through clues systematically:\n   - Clue (c): Ben drinks juice.\n   - Clue (d): Cleo does not drink tea \u2192 Cleo drinks either coffee or juice.\n   - But Ben drinks juice \u2192 Cleo doesn't drink juice \u2192 Cleo drinks coffee.\n   - Clue (b): Dog owner drinks coffee \u2192 Cleo owns the dog.\n   - Clue (a): Alice does not own fish.\n   So, Alice owns either cat or dog.\n   Since Cleo owns dog \u2192 Alice owns cat.\n   That leaves Ben with the fish.\n   So, Cleo owns the dog, and Ben owns the fish.\n   ANSWER 3: Cleo owns the dog; Ben owns the fish.\n\n4. Look at the sequence: 2, 6, 12, 20, 30.\n   Differences between terms: 4, 6, 8, 10.\n   These are increasing by 2 each time \u2192 next difference should be 12.\n   So, 30 + 12 = 42.\n   ANSWER 4: 42\n\n5. \"All but 9 die\" means 9 sheep survive.\n   ANSWER 5: 9\n\n6. Pipe A fills the tank in 6 hours \u2192 rate = 1/6 per hour.\n   Pipe B fills it in 3 hours \u2192 rate = 1/3 per hour.\n   Combined rate: 1/6 + 1/3 = 1/6 + 2/6 = 3/6 = 1/2 per hour.\n   Time to fill: 1 \u00f7 (1/2) = 2 hours.\n   ANSWER 6: 2\n\n7. A kilogram is exactly equal to 2.20462 pounds.\n   So a kilogram of feathers weighs more than a pound of steel.\n   ANSWER 7: A kilogram of feathers\n\n8. Let the original cost be C.\n   Retail price = C + 25% of C = 1.25C.\n   Sale price = 1.25C \u2212 20% of 1.25C = 1.25C \u00d7 0.8 = 1.00C.\n   Sale price is 100% of original cost.\n   ANSWER 8: 100%\n\n9. Let's consider both cases:\n   Case 1: X is a truth-teller.\n   Then, \"At least one of us is a liar\" is true \u2192 Y must be a liar.\n   This is consistent.\n   Case 2: X is a liar.\n   Then, \"At least one of us is a liar\" is false \u2192 both are truth-tellers.\n   But if X is a liar, he cannot tell the truth \u2014 contradiction.\n   Therefore, X is a truth-teller, and Y is a liar.\n   ANSWER 9: X is a truth-teller; Y is a liar\n\n10. Solve 3x + 7 = 2x + 15:\n   3x \u2212 2x = 15 \u2212 7 \u2192 x = 8.\n   ANSWER 10: 8\n\n11. Choose 3 from 5: C(5,3) = 5! / (3! \u00d7 2!) = 10.\n   ANSWER 11: 10\n\n12. Given:\n   - Dan > Ellie\n   - Ellie < Farah \u2192 Farah > Ellie\n   - Farah < Dan \u2192 Dan > Farah\n   So: Dan > Farah > Ellie.\n   Tallest: Dan, Shortest: Ellie.\n   ANSWER 12: Dan is tallest, Ellie is shortest", "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "context": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 678, 220, 16, 17, 5322, 3685, 13, 6928, 697, 975, 421, 498, 1366, 11, 714, 369, 94413, 3491, 11, 6248, 448, 198, 64, 1555, 304, 4063, 6823, 8932, 419, 3561, 320, 603, 817, 3491, 11, 304, 1973, 11, 518, 279, 1602, 835, 315, 697, 2033, 7731, 11692, 39351, 220, 16, 25, 366, 21732, 4226, 397, 11692, 39351, 220, 17, 25, 366, 21732, 4226, 397, 9338, 11692, 39351, 220, 16, 17, 25, 366, 21732, 4226, 1339, 1336, 21699, 1447, 16, 13, 362, 8061, 30778, 78531, 369, 400, 19, 1817, 323, 22601, 369, 400, 16, 13, 20, 15, 1817, 13, 23016, 49531, 220, 22, 78531, 323, 220, 16, 17, 22601, 11, 1221, 5221, 264, 220, 16, 15, 4, 11089, 389, 279, 2790, 13, 2585, 1753, 1558, 1340, 2291, 11, 304, 11192, 1939, 17, 13, 7355, 374, 10917, 438, 2310, 438, 78913, 572, 220, 21, 1635, 4134, 13, 758, 220, 19, 1635, 11, 7355, 686, 387, 220, 18, 15, 13, 2585, 2310, 374, 78913, 1431, 1939, 18, 13, 14513, 4780, 1959, 29405, 11, 7355, 11, 323, 36002, 78, 1959, 1817, 1828, 6896, 825, 6753, 320, 